From 55baeb7895963520d3e2da722a8facc62c5c82cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:27:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy: WarmongerHurry and NoObsoleteHurry into
 the bundle; no AI of ours ever buys a Warrior (the user's call)

The user: "I don't even want to test it, I just never want to see a civ
hurry a warrior again."
- WarmongerHurry: true in kCandidateFixes, unchanged otherwise.
- NoObsoleteHurry: true; it now also blocks every Warrior and unique
  replacement (unit class UNITCLASS_WARRIOR: Jaguar, Maori Warrior...),
  with or without Bronze Working. Moved from the hurry loop into the gold
  purchase check (CvEconomicAI::IsGoldPurchaseAllowed, called from
  CvCity::IsCanPurchase), so it covers every gold purchase path, like
  WarmongerHurry. Major AI civs only (city-states run all bundle flags).
- Blocks in a city in danger are logged as before, with the flag's name.
SettlerSaveRealistic and PeaceHurry stay off. On top of patch 0023.
Written 10:28am ET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
---
